TITLE      Radiative capture cross-sections for 3 MeV neutrons    30031  1    3 
AUTHOR     (G.Peto,Z.Milligy,I.Hunyadi)                           30031  1    4 
INSTITUTE  (3HUNDEB)                                              30031  1    5 
REFERENCE  (J,JNE,21,797,1967) Description expt, graphs,data table30031  1    6 
FACILITY   (CCW) 300keV locally built cascade accelerator         30031  1    7 
INC-SOURCE (D-D) Brass self-target, water cooled,direct deut-beam 30031  1    8 
           beam spot was 5 mm                                     30031  1    9 
SAMPLE     Solid samples were covered by thin polyethylene foils  30031  1   10 
           and were 18mm diameter                                 30031  1   11 
           target-sample distance 10-15 mm,                       30031  1   12 
           samples were placed at 0 deg.                          30031  1   13 
METHOD     (ACTIV) Activation                                     30031  1   14 
PART-DET   (B-,DG) Beta and gamma counting                        30031  1   15 
DETECTOR   (GEMUC) Mica end-window geiger muller counter          30031  1   16 
           neutron flux monitored with anthracene scintillator as 30031  1   17 
           well as bf3 long counter                               30031  1   18 
CORRECTION Intensities of thermal and epithermal neutrons were    30031  1   19 
           determined and also flux due to deuterons missing the  30031  1   20 
           target, deviations were statistical in origin          30031  1   21 
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) errors given include those due to standards 30031  1   22 
           react. uncertainty, beta counting error and statistics 30031  1   23 
ANALYSIS   for the decay schemes the data were taken from         30031  1   24 
           Nuclear Data Sheets(1961), the standards cross-sections30031  1   25 
           used are a best fit to measured and literature values  30031  1   26 
STATUS     (TABLE) Data taken from J.Nucl.Energy 21, 797, table 1 30031  1   27 
           (APRVD) Approved by Peto,letter (5/9/72)               30031  1   28 
